// Labelled goals for calibrating [run] ambiguity_threshold. See
// overmind/calibration.py for the format and for how to record scores.
//
// ambiguous = true means a competent engineer would have to ask a question
// before starting, and any answer they guessed could be the wrong one.
// ambiguous = false means the goal names its artifact and its finished state,
// even if the work itself is large.
//
// `score` is the planner's self-reported ambiguity and is null until recorded
// against a live coordinator. Do not fill these in by hand.
